      "q_source": "stage2_test_predictions.csv",
      "step_number": 1,
      "text": "Step 1: Let \\( c \\) be a root of the quadratic equation \\( x^2 + ax + b = 0 \\). Then, by definition, we have:\n\\[ c^2 + ac + b = 0. \\]",
      "z": -2.069830166165229
    },
    {
      "aligned_char_end": 401,
      "boundary_aligned_back": true,
      "char_end": 402,
      "char_start": 135,
      "effective_step": 2,
      "end_token_index": 177,
      "feature_source": "stage2_saved_hidden_states[19]",
      "near_end": false,
      "prefix_token_count": 178,
      "q": 0.4395893871185981,
      "q_source": "stage2_test_predictions.csv",
      "step_number": 2,
      "text": "Step 2: Since \\( c^2 - 2 \\) is also a root, it must satisfy the same quadratic equation:\n\\[ (c^2 - 2)^2 + a(c^2 - 2) + b = 0. \\]\nExpanding this, we get:\n\\[ c^4 - 4c^2 + 4 + ac^2 - 2a + b = 0. \\]\nRearranging terms, we obtain:\n\\[ c^4 + (a - 4)c^2 + (4 - 2a + b) = 0. \\]",
      "z": -0.24282867222464244
    },
    {
      "aligned_char_end": 508,
      "boundary_aligned_back": true,
      "char_end": 509,
      "char_start": 404,
      "effective_step": 3,
      "end_token_index": 232,
      "feature_source": "stage2_saved_hidden_states[19]",
      "near_end": false,
      "prefix_token_count": 233,
      "q": 0.3207996676479115,
      "q_source": "stage2_test_predictions.csv",
      "step_number": 3,
      "text": "Step 3: We now have two equations:\n1. \\( c^2 + ac + b = 0 \\)\n2. \\( c^4 + (a - 4)c^2 + (4 - 2a + b) = 0 \\)",
      "z": -0.750099284344198
    },
    {
      "aligned_char_end": 612,
      "boundary_aligned_back": true,
      "char_end": 613,
      "char_start": 511,
      "effective_step": 4,
      "end_token_index": 270,
      "feature_source": "stage2_saved_hidden_states[19]",
      "near_end": false,
      "prefix_token_count": 271,
      "q": 0.5477758579430563,
      "q_source": "stage2_test_predictions.csv",
      "step_number": 4,
      "text": "Step 4: From the first equation, express \\( b \\) in terms of \\( c \\) and \\( a \\):\n\\[ b = -c^2 - ac. \\]",
      "z": 0.19168823849893135
    },
    {
      "aligned_char_end": 841,
      "boundary_aligned_back": true,
      "char_end": 842,
      "char_start": 615,
      "effective_step": 5,
      "end_token_index": 389,
      "feature_source": "stage2_saved_hidden_states[19]",
      "near_end": false,
      "prefix_token_count": 390,
      "q": 0.7940950734478899,
      "q_source": "stage2_test_predictions.csv",
      "step_number": 5,
      "text": "Step 5: Substitute \\( b = -c^2 - ac \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ c^4 + (a - 4)c^2 + (4 - 2a - c^2 - ac) = 0. \\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[ c^4 + (a - 4)c^2 + 4 - 2a - c^2 - ac = 0, \\]\n\\[ c^4 + (a - 5)c^2 - ac + 4 - 2a = 0. \\]",
      "z": 1.3497886532736816
    },
    {
      "aligned_char_end": 1312,
      "boundary_aligned_back": true,
      "char_end": 1314,
      "char_start": 844,
      "effective_step": 6,
      "end_token_index": 537,
      "feature_source": "stage2_saved_hidden_states[19]",
      "near_end": false,
      "prefix_token_count": 538,
      "q": 0.875855824227121,
      "q_source": "stage2_test_predictions.csv",
      "step_number": 6,
      "text": "Step 6: For the above equation to hold for all roots \\( c \\), the coefficients of corresponding powers of \\( c \\) must be zero. Therefore, we set up the system of equations:\n1. The coefficient of \\( c^4 \\): \\( 1 = 0 \\) (which is always true and does not provide new information).\n2. The coefficient of \\( c^3 \\): \\( -a = 0 \\Rightarrow a = 0 \\).\n3. The coefficient of \\( c^2 \\): \\( a - 5 = 0 \\Rightarrow a = 5 \\).\n4. The constant term: \\( 4 - 2a = 0 \\Rightarrow a = 2 \\).",
      "z": 1.9537578951457464
    },
    {
      "aligned_char_end": 1579,
      "boundary_aligned_back": true,
      "char_end": 1580,
      "char_start": 1316,
      "effective_step": 7,
